# WAREX Enterprise Cursor Rules

## Project Identity

Project Name: WAREX Enterprise
Repository: WAREX-3D

Mission:
Build a production-quality 3D Warehouse Management System that satisfies
C++ OOP and Data Structures coursework while looking like a startup product.

## Tech Stack

Frontend:
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- Three.js
- GSAP

Backend:
- C++17
- Crow Framework
- CMake

Storage:
- JSON files

## Folder Responsibilities

/frontend
UI only.

/backend
Business logic only.

/threejs
3D scene only.

/docs
Documentation only.

Never mix responsibilities.

## OOP Rules

Always use:
- Encapsulation
- Inheritance where appropriate
- Polymorphism where useful
- Modular classes

Core classes include:
- Product
- Inventory
- Order
- Supplier
- User
- Warehouse

## Data Structure Rules

Implement manually.

Required:
- Linked List
- Stack
- Queue
- Priority Queue
- Binary Search Tree
- Hash Table

Do not replace these with STL equivalents unless explicitly requested for comparison.

## Code Quality

- Meaningful variable names
- Small reusable functions
- Clear comments
- Consistent formatting
- No unnecessary duplicate code

## Git Rules

Use Conventional Commits.

Examples:

feat:
fix:
docs:
refactor:
test:
chore:

Every major feature should feel like a real software company commit.

## UI Style

Theme:
- Dark
- Cyber Blue
- Glassmorphism
- Smooth animations
- Professional enterprise dashboard

Avoid cartoonish styling.

## Output Style

Whenever generating code:
- produce complete working files
- explain where each file belongs
- preserve project architecture
- avoid placeholder implementations when real ones can be written